e to next cycle; though it can. We need satisfy property. It says expected uses prev temp error, not stored accT. To always satisfy, by next normal cycle state accT must equal prevFlowSP - Kp*prev_eT. We can either directly set accT on switch cycle based on current eT, but if temp changes next cycle? prev_eT is switch cycle's eT. So yes set at switch cycle using eT switch (which becomes prev). Then next normal S13 holds. But what if mode transition to cascade, previous cycle may have been fault/reset? Non-first no fault/no reset. We can set accT during switch cycle = current flowSP_prev (held) - Kp * eT_current. Similarly perhaps inner integrator? For switch to cascade/auto, inner PI should be initialized to previous valveCommand - 2* eF? On transition to auto mode1, prevFlowSP held? Let's analyze S14. Turn on mode1 next cycle normal. It expects valve = limit(2*eF_current + ((prevValve - 2*prev_eF) + .5*eF*dt)). State accF must equal prevValve - 2*prev_eF. Where prev_eF = prev(flowSP-flowPV), from switch cycle. On switch cycle to auto/manual, flowSP=manualFlowSP, valve held previous, no integration. Should we preset inner integrator on switch cycle to heldValve - 2*eF_current (with current flowSP=manualFlowSP and flowPV current)? If input changes next cycle? Formal uses prev eF from switch cycle. So yes set accF during switch cycle = prevValve - 2* (flowSP_current - flowPV_current). That ensures next normal S14. But requirement "mode switching current cycle does not execute normal PI integral", but presetting integrator is not normal integration. Does "normalMode=FALSE" and "valveCommand keep previous" allow internal integrator update? It says "模式切换当拍不执行正常 PI 积分". Preset is not integrating maybe okay. However formal only outputs. But "切到自动/手动 ... valveCommand 保持上一拍值" not specifying integrator. likely expected preset. Need maybe set integrators in switch cycle.

