Now S13 formal expected:
`normalMode AND mode=2 -> flowSP equals LIMIT(0, 1*eT + ((prevFlowSP -1* prevET)+.2*eT*scanSeconds),50)`. Our normal mode2 calculation using accT. Need ensure `accT == prevFlowSP - 1*prevET` at start of normal mode2. Our state updates in transition/preset/manual/auto etc. Need examine all paths to mode2 stable.

Case mode2 stable across previous normal cycle:
At previous normal mode2 end, accT = prevFlowSP_at_end - 1*tempError_at_end. Next cycle temp inputs maybe current. In S13 prevET is previous cycle's tempError (same as tempError_at_end). Thus accT equals prevFlowSP-prevET. Good. Then rawFlow = 1*currentTempError + accT + .2*currentTempError*scanSeconds = exactly expected. Clamp. After clamp accT = flowSP-currentTempError. Good.
Case previous cycle mode2 switch (transition) with current mode2 later:
In switch cycle to mode2, flowSP=prevFlowSPBefore, valve=prevValveBefore, and we set accT = flowSP - Kp*currentTempError (switch cycle current). This becomes prevFlowSP - prevET for next cycle. Good.
