We set accT = flowSP_current - Kp*eT_current, where flowSP current output. If previous cycle was mode1 normal, output flowSP=manual. next cycle could mode2 only if mode changed, so that next cycle is a transition cycle, not normal; we will handle switch and set accT again based on held prev output instead of relying. Actually mode changed caught. If previous mode1 -> mode2, current is switch branch and sets accT to prevFlowSP - Kp*current eT, which is expected for following normal. Good.
If previous mode0/1 stable then mode2 same? not possible.
So S13 holds.

