Now consider `flowPV` input might change between switch and next normal. Formal S14 uses prev(flowSP-flowPV) from switch cycle, where flowPV switch. Our accF uses current flowPV switch cycle. good. If it changes next cycle, accF remains tied to prevEF, as expected.

Now what about `valveCommand` limit in manual, fault, first? manualValve guaranteed 0..100, okay. flowSP manual 0..50. S1/S2 always satisfied. In normal cascade, clamp. In mode1, raw valve clamp. In switch to mode2, prev outputs within limits from prior. good. In switch to auto/manual, flowSP manual within 0..50, valve previous within 0..100; S2. Good. In all branches flowSP/valve within limits. S1/S2 invariant.

Need ensure outputs are declared outputs. Assign.

Potential CODESYS reserved local identifiers `s` and `r`: avoid.

Use `LIMIT`? We'll manual clamp, but numerous IF. Could use helper functions? Instruction says no nested FUNCTION/METHOD/ACTION. So inline.

We can implement clamp using:
IF rawFlow < 0.0 THEN
    flowSP := 0.0;
ELSIF rawFlow > 50.0 THEN
    flowSP := 50.0;
